; [0.8.1-RT14] (#954), work #955: Style of -ATTDEF (card PT14, "Le domande del testo",
; point 4; decision on #954 and on the review of #1026, point 3). A name that does not
; exist and "?" give "Cannot find text style "<name>"." and the question repeats; ARIAL,
; as TENSIONE of autocad-attributi, becomes the current style, and the repeated line says
; "ARIAL". The change of style is part of the Attdef step (card PT14, point 3): U takes
; the ATTDEF away and Standard is current again; REDO brings both back.
; Source: Matleyx78/dxf-test-file, commit 2aafbb1fa17abc67fdf2ff7de26a34b70e79b736
; (CC0-1.0): autocad-attributi.txt (AutoCAD 2021, Italian, translated as docs/adr/0056,
; point 2, and card PT14). The ARIAL style is made with -STYLE and the prompts of
; style/cambia-esistente and text/stile-altezza-fissa, then Standard is made current
; again; the ARIAL record takes handle 257.
; ~box (docs/adr/0022): LiberationSans-Regular.ttf of resources/fonts, read with a small
; reader of its head, hhea, OS/2, cmap and hmtx tables: cap height 1409, ascent 1854,
; descent -434, summed advances; an ATTDEF shows its tag. arial.ttf is Liberation Sans.
